---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SideMenu from '../sanctuary/SideMenu.astro';
import ItchButton from '../project/ItchButton.astro';
import cover from '@assets/stellar-strays/cover.jpg';

const menuLinks = [
  { label: 'OVERVIEW', href: '#top' },
  { label: 'CONTRIBUTION', href: '#contribution' },
  { label: 'CHARACTER DESIGN', href: '#character-design' },
  { label: 'ANIMATION', href: '#animation' },
  { label: 'ASSETS DESIGN', href: '#assets-design' },
  { label: 'CONTACT', href: '#contact' },
];
---

<section class="hero grid-1440" id="top">
  <SideMenu links={menuLinks} />

  <div class="inner">
    <h1>Stellar Strays</h1>
    <p class="type">Team project · Game Lab course · 2025</p>

    <div class="trailer">
      <Image src={cover} alt="Fermi and Rumba in Stellar Strays" widths={[600, 900, 1400]} sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 70vw, 894px" loading="eager" />
    </div>

    <div class="cols info">
      <div class="gc-1-3">
        <h3 class="p-label">Project description</h3>
        <div class="after-label">
          <p class="p-text">
            Stellar Strays is a local co-op platformer for two players. Astronaut Fermi and
            repair-bot Rumba have crash-landed on one of two neighboring planets, and now they have
            to find the parts of their ship, scattered across floating islands with gravity of
            their own, to repair it and continue their journey.
          </p>
          <p class="p-text">
            The players have to act together: many hard-to-reach places can only be reached by
            coordinating their moves. The ship parts are divided between the two characters too.
            Some can only be collected by Rumba, because their sound waves would hurt Fermi’s
            sensitive ears, and others only by Fermi, because their electric field would short out
            Rumba.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ItchButton href="https://ksenia-spirina.itch.io/stellar-strays" />
      </div>
      <div class="gc-5-3">
        <h3 class="p-label">Credits</h3>
        <div class="after-label">
          <p class="p-text keep-host">
            Stellar Strays was created as an assignment in the course “Game&nbsp;Lab”, a
            collaboration between the
            <span class="keep-name">Visual <span class="keep-always">Communication Department</span></span> of
            <span class="keep-name"><span class="keep-always">Bezalel Academy of Arts and</span> Design</span> and
            Hebrew&nbsp;University, 2025.
          </p>
          <p class="p-text"><strong>Programming:</strong> Idan Baras, David Feldman, Roy Mor</p>
          <p class="p-text"><strong>Art and Design:</strong> Maayan Berkovits, Ksenia Spirina</p>
          <p class="p-text"><strong>Guidance:</strong> Yuval Markovich, Danielle Mossak, Omer Zadok</p>
          <p class="p-text"><strong>Assistance:</strong> Sagie Levy</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: calc(128px - var(--nav-height));
    padding-bottom: 128px;
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 1rem);
  }

  .inner {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #4361ee;
  }

  .type {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: #9a9a9a;
  }

  @supports (text-box-trim: trim-both) {
    h1 {
      text-box: trim-end cap alphabetic;
    }

    .type {
      margin-top: 32px;
      text-box: trim-start cap alphabetic;
    }
  }

  .trailer {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 894px;
    aspect-ratio: 894 / 503;
    margin-top: 64px;
    background: rgba(217, 217, 217, 0.1);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .trailer :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .info {
    margin-top: 96px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }

    .type {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
